hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"299","Muhammad bin Uzair Al-Ayli told us that Salamah bin Ruh told them, on the authority of Uqail, who said: Muhammad bin Muslim told me that Ubayd Allah bin Abd Allah ibn Utba informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas informed him that Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him that One day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a state of grief and disapproving of what was seen of him, so I asked him about what I disapproved of, and he said to her: Gabriel promised me that he would meet me tonight, but I did not see him, but by God, he did not leave me behind.” Maimouna said: “And in my house there was a dog puppy under a table.” For us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it out, then sprinkled its place with water with his hand.” When night fell, Gabriel met him and said to him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “You promised me, and then I did not see you?” Gabriel said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: We do not enter a house in which \A picture or a dog\"""""
